The supplied float semantics is tailored to this exact pattern: it explicitly supports float subtraction/division and documents that symbolic float-list `min`/`max` should be intercepted in `verification.k` with opaque extrema summaries. I’m using the canonical implementation—compute both extrema once, then map `(x - min) / (max - min)`—and will make the proof state its structural postcondition over arbitrary float-list tails.
